==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|čьrnъ|lang=ru}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|kr̥snós|black|lang=ru}}. Cognates include Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrs|чрънъ|tr=črŭnŭ||black|lang=cu}}, Bulgarian {{term|черен|lang=bg}}, Serbo-Croatian {{term|црн|lang=sh}}/{{term|crn|lang=sh}}, Slovene {{term|črn|lang=sl}}, Slovak {{term|čierny|lang=sk}}; Norwegian and Swedish {{term|harr||grayling|lang=sv}}, Sanskrit {{term|कृष्ण|tr=kṛṣṇá|sc=Deva|lang=sa}}, Old Prussian {{term|kirsnan||black|lang=prg}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-чёрный.ogg|audio}}
* {{IPA|[ˈʨɵrnɨj]|lang=ru}}

===Adjective===
{{head|ru|adjective|tr=čórnyj}}

# [[black]]
# [[rough]], [[coarse]]
# [[back]] ''(stairs, entrance, etc.)''
# ''(labor)'': [[unskilled]], [[manual]]
# ''(metal)'': [[ferrous]]
#:* {{Cyrl|[[на]] чёрный [[день]]}} — ''for a rainy day''
#:* {{Cyrl|чёрным [[по]] [[белый|бе́лому]]}} — ''in black and white''
#:* {{Cyrl|чёрное [[дерево|де́рево]]}} — ''ebony''
#:* {{Cyrl|чёрная [[доска|доска́]]}} — ''blackboard''
#:* {{Cyrl|чёрная [[металлургия|металлу́ргия]]}} — ''iron and steel industry''

